n’s groups. However, after World War II, she lost her teaching job because of her Nazi background, although she later became a librarian. The " [:a {:href "/results/58141"} "1932"] " champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/77792"} "Lillian Copeland"] ", was Jewish and personally boycotted the 1936 Olympics to protest the Nazis not allowing Jews to compete on their Olympic team."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Distance"] [:th {} "Round #1 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #2 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #3 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #4 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #5 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #6 Distance"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "877"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70056"} "Gisela Mauermayer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "47.63"] [:td {} "47.63"] [:td {} "41.64"] [:td {} "40.70"] [:td {} "36.27"] [:td {} "43.54"] [:td {} "44.26"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "553"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/74662"} "Jadwiga Wajs"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} "46.22"] [:td {} "44.69"] [:td {} "31.99"] [:td {} "46.22"] [:td {} "43.36"] [:td {} "x"] [:td {} "42.89"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "878"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/70062"} "Paula Mollenhauer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: 